      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-149348",
      ":question/problem": "The integral\n\n$A = \\displaystyle \\int_{a}^{-0.435}f(x)dx$\n\nrepresents the (signed) area of the finite region bounded by the curve $f(x) = x^{7} + 3x^{2} - x - 1$ and the coordinate axes in the second quadrant. Find the lower limit $a$ to $3$ decimal places, and use your answer to estimate the area $A$.\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
